[{"step":1,"file":"ext/mbstring/tests/bug72710.phpt","function":"<global>","line":8,"var":"pattern","code":"mb_ereg('(?<0>a)', 'a');","note":"The attacker supplies an invalid named-group pattern directly to mb_ereg, forcing the regex compiler down its error-handling path."},{"step":2,"file":"ext/mbstring/php_mbregex.c","function":"PHP_FUNCTION(mb_ereg)","line":0,"var":"pattern","code":"mb_ereg forwards the supplied pattern into php_mbregex_compile_pattern and Oniguruma","note":"The malformed pattern reaches Oniguruma's parser through the shared mbregex compilation path."},{"step":3,"file":"ext/mbstring/php_mbregex.c","function":"_php_mb_regex_ereg_exec","line":900,"var":"re","code":"re = php_mbregex_compile_pattern(arg_pattern, arg_pattern_len, options, MBREX(current_mbctype), MBREX(regex_default_syntax));","note":"Compilation is the key entry point where the vulnerable AST analysis and error cleanup run."},{"step":4,"file":"oniguruma/src/regcomp.c","function":"tune_quant","line":5458,"var":"qn->emptiness","code":"qn->emptiness = quantifiers_memory_node_info(body);","note":"The compiler's recursive analysis is invoked while building the regex AST, and malformed constructs can perturb this path."},{"step":5,"file":"oniguruma/src/regcomp.c","function":"quantifiers_memory_node_info","line":4894,"var":"node","code":"static enum BodyEmptyType quantifiers_memory_node_info(Node* node)","note":"This recursive AST walk is the suspected root cause path from the crash report, matching the reported state names."},{"step":6,"file":"oniguruma/src/regcomp.c","function":"quantifiers_memory_node_info","line":4904,"var":"NODE_CAR(node)","code":"v = quantifiers_memory_node_info(NODE_CAR(node));","note":"Nested list/alt nodes are traversed recursively, so malformed nested patterns can force repeated visits through the same subtree."},{"step":7,"file":"oniguruma/src/regcomp.c","function":"quantifiers_memory_node_info","line":4949,"var":"en->te.Then","code":"v = quantifiers_memory_node_info(en->te.Then);","note":"Conditional subtrees are also recursively analyzed, increasing the chance of hitting the vulnerable optimizer path with complex patterns."},{"step":8,"file":"ext/mbstring/php_mbregex.c","function":"PHP_FUNCTION(mb_ereg)","line":0,"var":"MBREX(search_re)","code":"On compile failure, mbregex error handling must unwind partially built state","note":"The bug report indicates the crash occurs during compile-error cleanup, not normal matching."},{"step":9,"file":"ext/mbstring/php_mbregex.c","function":"PHP_FUNCTION(mb_ereg)","line":0,"var":"return_value","code":"mb_ereg returns after compile error handling","note":"If the cleanup path is buggy, the memory-safety sink is reached before PHP can return the warning."}]